{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"upbeat-illadvised-springtail","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context\nThe deprecation repair on dragonish-sylphic-sheep preserves rebar’s current Chat Completions wire behavior with the explicit `openai-chat:` prefix. Pydantic AI v2 makes the Responses API the default for `openai:`, so rebar should migrate deliberately after proving compatibility rather than inherit the semantic change implicitly.\n\n## Plan\n- Inventory every OpenAI and OpenAI-compatible endpoint, including custom base URLs, structured output, streaming, tool calls, retries, and provider-specific settings.\n- Define the supported Responses API contract and document any endpoints or features that remain Chat-Completions-only.\n- Add provider contract tests that compare current behavior with `openai-responses:` through production model construction.\n- Migrate eligible providers explicitly, add compatibility handling for ineligible custom endpoints, and document the operator-facing configuration change.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A provider capability matrix identifies each supported OpenAI-compatible endpoint as Responses-ready or Chat-Completions-only, with cited evidence.\n- [ ] Contract tests exercise real pydantic-ai model construction and assert structured output, streaming, tool-call, retry, and custom-base-URL behavior.\n- [ ] Eligible provider paths use `openai-responses:` explicitly; any retained `openai-chat:` path has a documented compatibility reason.\n- [ ] Configuration and migration documentation explain observable wire-semantic changes and rollback behavior.\n- [ ] Focused provider tests plus `make test`, `make lint`, and `make typecheck` pass.","id":"155c-218b-c128-4700","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":["pydantic-ai","provider","migration"],"ticket_type":"story","title":"Migrate OpenAI providers to the pydantic-ai Responses API"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787017356659244001,"uuid":"03b6a530-40f4-4169-8f6a-165f3b8c8b65"}